{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 17:03:07","profile":{"player_id":"136728","last_updated":"12/11/2026 17:03","fullname":"Lakshya Rajesh Raichandani","short_display_name":"L Raichandani","name":"Lakshya Raichandani","gender":"M","dob":"15/10/2008","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"","nationality_id":"4","nationality":"India","nationality_short_code":"IND","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"1","text":"Batsman","role":"Batter"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"7","text":"Off break"},"writeup":"<p>Lakshya Raichandani is a right-handed opening batter from Uttarakhand who bowls right-arm off-spin. Known for his defensive technique and shot judgment outside off-stump, he has established himself through long innings in multi-day cricket.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>He made his Ranji Trophy debut for Uttarakhand during the 2025-26 domestic season. In that campaign, he scored 223 runs across five innings, registering half-centuries against Bengal (86) and Karnataka (55) in the knockouts.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Raichandani made his international youth debut for India Under-19 in July 2026 during the tour of Sri Lanka. In the first Youth Test at Galle, he scored 207 off 324 balls, building a 295-run opening partnership with Sagar Virk to help India post 576. He added a second-innings century (100 off 116 balls) in the second Youth Test at Colombo.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>In September 2026, Raichandani was appointed captain for the Youth ODI series and vice-captain for the Youth Tests against Australia Under-19. During the series, he scored 110 in the third Youth ODI at Rajkot, followed by a career-best 240 off 281 balls in the first Youth Test, which set up an innings victory for India.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Lakshya is firmly established as one of India's premier young red-ball opening batters while steadily expanding his range in white-ball cricket. His technical discipline makes him a natural fit for multi-day cricket, while his evolving strokeplay gives him the tools to adapt to ODI and T20 cricket.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"1163","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"India Under-19"},{"id":"1668","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Uttarakhand"},{"id":"1890","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"India A Under-19"},{"id":"5228","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Rishikesh River Kings"}]},"international_debut":null,"international_last_match":null,"stats":{"format":[{"comp_type_id":"21","comp_type":"Youth Test","debut":{"match_id":"271826","match_date":"13/07/2026","for":{"id":"1163","text":"India Under-19","short_name":"IND-U19"},"vs":{"id":"1165","text":"Sri Lanka Under-19","short_name":"SL-U19"},"venue":{"id":"56","text":"Galle International Stadium, Galle"}},"last_match":{"match_id":"270987","match_date":"05/10/2026","for":{"id":"1163","text":"India Under-19","short_name":"IND-U19"},"vs":{"id":"1154","text":"Australia Under-19","short_name":"AUS-U19"},"venue":{"id":"2738","text":"Narendra Modi Stadium Ground A, Motera, Ahmedabad"}},"rankings":{"bat":null,"bat_rating":"0","bowl":null,"bowl_rating":"0","allrounder":null,"allrounder_rating":"0","bat_rank_change":null,"bowl_rank_change":null,"allrounder_rank_change":null},"overall":{"batting_record":{"matches":"4","innings":"6","not_outs":"2","runs":"557","balls_faced":"750","three_hundreds":"0","two_hundreds":"2","hundreds":"3","fifties":"0","fours":"57","sixes":"8","average":"139.25","strike_rate":"74.27","hs":{"score":{"is_no":"false","balls_faced":"281","text":"240"},"match_id":"270986","match_date":"27/09/2026","vs":{"id":"1154","text":"Australia Under-19","short_name":"AUS-U19"}}},"bowling_record":null,"fielding_record":{"catches":"11","stumpings":"0","run_outs":"0"}},"performance_by_year":{"year":[{"year_id":2026,"batting_record":{"runs":"557","balls_faced":"750","fift